+
+## Voyage 2: Browser acceptance defect repair
+
+**Defect source:** External Cypress acceptance suite reports 5 failures. The in-harness cucumber suite passes because happy-dom re-queries the DOM after each action. The real browser holds element references across chained commands, and those references break when the app rebuilds the list.
+
+**Root cause (tests 1-4):** `render()` in `js/app.js` rebuilds the entire `<ul class="todo-list">` via `innerHTML` on every state change (toggle, toggle-all, edit-save). Existing DOM nodes are destroyed and replaced. Cypress chained commands fail on stale references.
+
+**Root cause (test 5):** The `todomvc-app-css` package is not installed, so no CSS rule hides `.view` during `.editing` mode. The toggle checkbox remains visible.
+
+**Specs written:** `specs/dom-identity.feature` (W7) pins DOM-node preservation across toggle and toggle-all. `specs/editing-visibility.feature` (W8) pins control visibility during editing.
+
+**New watchbill targets:** W7-dom-identity, W8-editing-visibility. Both require new step definitions and production fixes.
