@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Feature: DOM identity preservation
+  As a user interacting with my todo list
+  I want DOM elements to persist across state changes
+  So that the interface remains stable during interaction
+
+  Rule: State changes mutate existing DOM nodes
+
+    Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves its DOM node
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on the "Buy milk" todo
+      Then the "Buy milk" todo DOM node is the same element
+      And the "Buy milk" todo is completed
+
+    Scenario: Toggling all todos preserves every DOM node
+      Given a todo titled "Buy milk" exists as active
+      And a todo titled "Buy eggs" exists as active
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then every todo DOM node is the same element
+      And the "Buy milk" todo is completed
+      And the "Buy eggs" todo is completed
